## Key Learnings

1. In Pekko v1.7.1 `Behavior.validateAsInitial` rejects only the `same` and `unhandled` tags, so a deferred or stopped behavior is not rejected by it (`Behavior.scala:240-243`).
2. Pekko's Typed `MailboxSelector.bounded(capacity)` is built as a Classic `BoundedMailbox(capacity, Duration.Zero)`, the same zero push-timeout variant as ADR 0030 D2 (`Mailboxes.scala:231-235`).
3. Typed `restartWithBackoff` applies the random factor after capping the exponential term, so the computed delay can exceed `maxBackoff` by up to `randomFactor` (`Supervision.scala:185-196`).
4. Typed timers belong to the actor context and survive behavior replacement; only restart, stop, cancel and same-key replacement invalidate them (`TimerSpec.scala:174-306`).
5. A Typed `unstash` that ends in a stopped or failed behavior sends the remaining messages to dead letters, while an exception keeps them in the buffer and an unhandled result continues replay (`StashBufferImpl.scala:187-252`).
